# Python & ML Patterns

## Python (this stack)
- Type hints on public signatures; prefer Pydantic/TypedDict at boundaries; avoid `Any`
- Ruff for lint/format; Google-style docstrings on public APIs
- Specific exceptions + context; `with` for resources; async only for I/O (no blocking in async)

## Pandas
- Vectorize; `.loc`/`.iloc` (no chained `[][]`); method-chain transforms; `.copy()` on slices
- Categoricals for low-cardinality strings; select columns early; set dtypes on read

## ML
- Pin seeds (`random_state`); YAML experiment config committed with results
- Temporal splits for time series — never random-split the future into train
- No target/future leakage; log params/metrics/artifacts

## Notebooks
- Markdown WHY before HOW; one logical op per cell; restart-and-run-all before commit
- `pathlib` relative paths; plots: whitegrid, DPI 150, tight bbox
